      "id": "2067018861833224664",
      "text": "Stop making prompts.\nStart designing loops.\nLoop engineering is the new meta.😗\n\nBoris Cherny (Claude Code at Anthropic) and others no longer “prompt” they design loops that prompt themselves.\n\nA loop is a self-running system with memory, automation, isolation, and objective checks.\n\nA single prompt gives you one response. A well-designed loop gives you a system that keeps working long after you close your laptop.\n\n6 key pieces of every working AI agent loop:\n\n1. Automations (triggers that run without you)\n2. Memory files ( STATE.md that survives runs)\n3. Worktrees (isolation so agents don’t collide)\n4. Skills & sub-agents\n5. Evaluator-optimizer pattern (writer vs checker)\n6. Hard stop conditions (not the AI says it’s done)\n\nThis is how you go from chatty AI to production-grade systems.\n\nThis is the exact shift top engineers at Anthropic are making right now.",
