    {
      "id": "2063883301278924857",
      "text": "A loop without memory starts from zero every run.\nA loop with memory remembers every mistake and repeats it.\nA loop that learns turns those mistakes into rules it has to follow.\n\nMine spent weeks as the second one.\n\nYour job is not designing loops that prompt your agents. It's designing loops that learn from experience.",
      "author": {
        "id": "1459767830623178755",
        "name": "Paweł Huryn",
        "screenName": "PawelHuryn",
        "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2049244285313359872/geQuKlQP_normal.jpg",
        "verified": true
